      },
      "text": "Lake Titicaca to La Paz"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "8c58ddf5b65152807acf6707fd60aa356a21001f893fcd5c2ba8771aa277decb",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-63081f33d4c840e99362579a12d8b39a",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast with views of the blue waters of Lake Titicaca, a short transfer takes you to Cocotoni Bay. From there, you’ll travel by hydrofoil to the Island of the Moon and visit Iñak Uyu, the Temple of the Virgins of the Sun. It is one of the lake’s sacred sites. The visit focuses on the role of women in Inca culture and their contributions to weaving, farming, religious traditions and food preparation, including the making of chuño and tunta. Look for the temple’s distinctive trapezoidal and stepped features.\n\nThe hydrofoil then continues to the Island of the Sun. You’ll visit the Great Inca Stairway and the Sacred Spring. According to local belief, its waters bestow youth and happiness. Lunch is at the Uma Kollu archaeological restaurant, near a small craft market.\n\nFrom the island, you’ll cross the lake to Copacabana. The visit includes the basilica, the Sanctuary of the Black Madonna and the local market. You’ll then continue overland to La Paz, taking a ferry across the Strait of Tiquina. Much of the road runs alongside the snow-capped peaks of the Andes."
    },
